# Dispatch Agent Conventions

Read `AGENTS.md` first for the pillar router and global invariants. This rule captures the
day-to-day coding conventions that must hold for every change.

## Scope discipline
- The task is infrastructure, not app features. Never change `apps/web/src` app logic.
- Backend edits are allowed only when infra needs them (e.g. `/api/live` probe endpoint).
- Prefer editing existing files over adding new ones; keep changes small and reviewable.

## Kubernetes / Helm
- Every container sets `requests` AND `limits`, runs non-root, and drops all capabilities.
  Reuse the `dispatch.containerSecurity` helper — do not inline security contexts.
- No `:latest` in manifests; images come from `values.yaml` (`kind load`ed `:local`, GHCR by SHA in CI).
- Labels via `dispatch.commonLabels`; selectors via `dispatch.selectorLabels`. Names via `dispatch.componentName`.
- Probes: readiness = `/api/health` (dependency-aware, 503 when Redis/Mongo down);
  liveness/startup = `/api/live` (dependency-free). Readiness and liveness must differ.
- Secrets live only in the `Secret` (injected via `envFrom`), never in the `ConfigMap`.
- Validate chart changes with `helm lint` + `helm template` before claiming done.

## Bootstrap script (`run-platform.sh`)
- K8s path is the default (`up` = cluster -> deps -> deploy -> smoke); compose is `compose-*` fallback.
- Fail fast in preflight with actionable hints. Keep functions small and single-purpose.
- Run Python tooling from the `.tmp/infra-venv` venv — never `pip install` into system Python.

## Infra tests (`tests/infra`, pytest)
- Drive smoke/e2e through the Ingress host over HTTPS, never `kubectl port-forward`.
- Cluster-state tests assert against the k8s API (readiness, probes, resources, secrets, HPA, ingress).
- 4-space indentation, standard-library first; avoid adding dependencies for trivial parsing (e.g. parse SSE by hand).

## Comments & style
- Comment the "why" (trade-offs, constraints), never narrate the "what".
- Record every non-obvious decision in `docs/conventions.md`; surface it in the README matrix.
